    "createdAt": "2025-10-30T19:09:30.420847+00:00",
    "curatorComment": "<p>I remember buying the first issue of Astro City when it came out back in 1995. (Yes, I'm very old.) As a lifelong comics reader, I had enjoyed Kurt Busiek's work on Avengers (and other books) and was excited to see this new title.</p><p>What I love about Astro City is that at a time when Image Comics was thriving on the strength of large-than-life, over-the-top takes on superheroes (as in Spawn, Youngblood, etc.), Astro City was about the personal stories that took place in the background.</p><p>That first issue asks what a Superman would dream of. A man with immense power and immense responsibility dreams of flying free, without the need to save everyone, just for a little bit. And it only gets better from there.</p><p>If you haven't read Astro City before, you're in for a treat. And if you have, do what I did when Image released these Metrobooks - binge it all again!</p><p>-Dignan</p>",
    "curatorStatement": null,
